WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.432
Agent decisions should be structured.

00:00:02.432 --> 00:00:11.002
If the controller only needs to know the next route, do not ask the model for a long paragraph explaining what it feels

00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:11.382
like doing.

00:00:11.382 --> 00:00:19.887
A weak output might say, I think perhaps we should search the policy because the user seems to be asking about returns.

00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:23.980
That is difficult for application code to interpret reliably.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:32.227
A better result is a small object with a route and, if useful, a short visible reason.

00:00:32.227 --> 00:00:39.167
For example: route equals policy search; reason equals the question asks about return rules.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:43.651
This is easier to validate, log, test, and route.

00:00:44.306 --> 00:00:48.083
Also remember that an L L M is not always necessary.

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:52.668
If a normal if statement can make the decision correctly, use it.

00:00:52.668 --> 00:00:59.248
Structured model decisions are most useful when the user's language is ambiguous enough to justify semantic

00:00:59.248 --> 00:01:00.284
interpretation.
